### Amendment 3

The same S1 model, after the bound above, was checked to completion. TLC reported no invariant violation: 46,585 distinct states, depth 25, about 6 seconds. The fingerprint line was `val = 2.9E-10`. The runner printed `UNEXPLAINED bound` because it treated every positive probability as a missed check. That reading of TLC was wrong. TLC prints the probability at the end of every completed check, and for a state space this size the probability is a tiny positive number. The runner now treats a probability below `1e-3`, with "No error has been found", as a finished check. A probability at or above `1e-3`, or a run stopped by the memory cap, remains `UNEXPLAINED bound`. This amendment is informed by that log, not by an invariant counterexample. The predictions are unchanged."}

